{{Quote|What's your house?''"<br />"''I'm Clan Wren, House Vizsla.|A [[Journeyman Protector|Mandalorian Protector]] and [[Sabine Wren]]|<ref name="Protector of Concord Dawn">{{Rebels|The Protector of Concord Dawn}}</ref>}}
In the [[Mandalorian]] culture, families were referred to as '''clans'''. Clans often presided over their own fiefdoms and were usually vassals of a "[[Mandalorian house|house]]," or [[Politics|political]] faction.<ref name="Protector Recon">{{RebelsRecon|Ob90p0SoMpY|#2.19: Inside "The Mystery of Chopper Base" &#124; Star Wars Rebels|sw_url=video/rebels-recon-inside-the-mystery-of-chopper-base}}</ref> For example, members of [[Clan Wren]], who ruled the [[planet]] [[Krownest]], were allied with [[House Vizsla]].<ref name="Protector of Concord Dawn" /> Other clans included [[Clan Awaud]],<ref name="Friends Like These">''[[Friends Like These]]''</ref> [[Clan Eldar]], [[Clan Kryze]], [[Clan Rook]],<ref name="Heroes of Mandalore">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Heroes of Mandalore]]''</ref> [[Clan Saxon]],<ref name="DB Clan Saxon">{{Databank|clan-saxon|Clan Saxon}}</ref> [[Clan Verminoth]],<ref name="Cly Kullervo">{{Databank|cly-kullervo|Cly Kullervo}}</ref> and [[Clan Vizsla]].<ref name="Shades">{{TCW|Shades of Reason}}</ref> [[The Tribe]] was a clan,<ref name="Armored and Ready Armorer">{{Topps|set=2022 Topps Star Wars: The Mandalorian Chrome|subset=Armored & Ready|cardname=The Armorer}}</ref> with [[Clan Mudhorn]] growing out of it.<ref name="Chapter 8">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 8: Redemption}}</ref> Members of the [[Mandalorian Guard]] were recruited from every clan.<ref name="Starfighters">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles]]''</ref>

{{Mando-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The structure of Mandalorian society was first explicitly described by [[Dave Filoni]], former supervising director of the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' TV series and executive producer on the following series ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]''. Following the release of the ''Rebels'' episode "[[The Protector of Concord Dawn]]," Filoni explained that the Mandalorian society is pyramidal: it has a ruler, big factions known as houses, and familial units (clans) allied with said houses.

